<title>HUNGARY: Tietmeyer says Europe debate factor in dollar rise.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer says Europe debate factor in dollar rise.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said in an interview recorded on Monday and due to be broadcast in Hungary next week that concerns over future European integration were a factor in the dollar's recent rise.</p>
<p>&quot;It could be the case that in the present development one or the other critical attitude towards European development is a factor included (in the dollar's rise),&quot; he told Hungarian radio.</p>
</text>
